00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.290
It's going to be about what you
need to do in your workplace

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.660
to actually stand out and be
perceived by the senior leaders

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.660
and thought leaders in your organization,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.900
as actually somebody who really adds value

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.040
to your team and your organization.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.110
Visibility is a key concept that you need

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.620
to understand in order to advance

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.060
in any corporate organization of any kind.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.200
So hang in here with me,
it's going to be interesting

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.800
it's going to be very important.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.330
So once again welcome
to another coffee break

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.460
with Firm Learning, my name is Heinrich,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.010
and today we talk about visibility.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.300
Visibility is really a game changer.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.350
Visibility can make or break your career.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.220
So it's super crucial and important

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.580
that you understand what
visibility is all about.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.390
And the reason why I chose this topic

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.060
for this video is the following,

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.360
I recently thought back
about a conversation I had

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.530
with some colleagues
at an internship I did

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.670
at a tech consulting
company, many many years ago.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.880
I was still in university,
still in my undergrad.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.150
And I was working at a large
German DAX Corporation,

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.490
it's the big blue chip
stock index in Germany.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.810
And this consulting firm was
working for this large company,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.880
so we were on the client
side almost every day.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.770
So I noticed that in a
period of a couple of weeks

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.140
all of the colleagues were
getting a bit more nervous,

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.300
there were some kind of
a tension in the room

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.692
that I didn't observe in the
earlier weeks of my internship.

00:01:41.692 --> 00:01:44.020
So I asked a bit around, what is going on?

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.830
And I learned that actually
now it was designation season,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:49.970
so they had a process where
two or three times a year,

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.690
each colleague got evaluated

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.490
and if they matched certain criteria,

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.580
both regarding tenure but
also regarding performance,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.610
they would be designated
to the next level.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.120
And then of course would
get a higher salary,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.410
more benefits, and so on.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.110
And this was obviously a big thing

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.730
for everybody in the company.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.610
So everybody was a bit nervous, of course,

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.600
trying to make the very best impression

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.070
at work at this time.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.000
Trying to perform as good as they could.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.910
And then I overheard a conversation

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.731
that two of the more senior
colleagues on the team had,

00:02:18.731 --> 00:02:21.347
which really made me think.

00:02:21.347 --> 00:02:25.550
And this conversation they
had was about visibility.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.550
And what do I mean by that, what happened?

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.610
Well, they were talking
about another client

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.770
on the team who is a bit more junior,

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.557
and they were discussing
him, and they were saying

00:02:34.557 --> 00:02:38.117
"Hey, this guy, he is a good
guy, he's doing good work,

00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:40.120
"but he's just not visible enough."

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.630
This is what they were saying.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.947
So they were doubting
if he would make the cut

00:02:43.947 --> 00:02:45.950
and actually get the promotion.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.020
And for me this for
something completely new.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.400
Of course I was very young,
and maybe also a bit naive,

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.810
and the way I was thinking about the work

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.940
was that well, if you do a good job,

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.600
at some point this is
going to be recognized,

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.536
and then at some point your
team lead, or your supervisor,

00:03:01.536 --> 00:03:04.506
would pick you and then you designate you.

00:03:04.506 --> 00:03:07.360
And then this is how you
advance in your career.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.010
Do the job as good as you
can, and this would be enough.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.920
But the reality is it's not
always working like that.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.228
This is far too simplistic
to really describe

00:03:17.228 --> 00:03:19.730
how these kind of things work, and happen,

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.900
in especially larger corporations.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.040
But I trust this is not very different

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.450
in most smaller sized
corporations as well.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.060
And yes of course, doing a good job,

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.880
having a good and stellar performance

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:33.610
at the things that you do,
is of course important,

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:36.720
and will make a difference
in one way or the other

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.710
how far you get in your career.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:41.520
I think it doesn't
matter how much politics

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.236
are going on in a company, in the end,

00:03:44.236 --> 00:03:47.630
how good you do your job will always

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:51.110
somehow influence your chances
in terms of getting along,

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.230
and doing then the next
step in your career.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.830
But, and I think this
is a very basic truth,

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.390
that it's probably hard to understand

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.710
for many new joiners, people
just starting out in business,

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.160
it is not enough.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.659
Other concepts, for instance visibility,

00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:06.795
is very, very important.

00:04:06.795 --> 00:04:10.330
And let me give you an example
of how that could play out,

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.120
why that might be important.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.610
So if you think about how these
designation processes work

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:18.130
in all companies, and of
course here are differences

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.330
from company here to company.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.360
But in general this works is that

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.010
once or twice every year,
the HR community will meet

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.220
with the business leaders
of the organization,

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.605
and they will ask themselves the question,

00:04:28.605 --> 00:04:32.160
okay, whom can I designate
to the next level?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.720
Who makes the cut to now
advance to the next position?

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.150
And yes, of course, this
is probably more like this

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.110
in roles like consulting or banking,

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.970
where you have this cycle of
constantly being designated

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.100
every couple of years
if you're good enough.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.950
Maybe this is slightly
different in an industry

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.040
where it's more opportunity based,

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.900
if there's now a role that is opening up,

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.230
but then people ask themselves,

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.410
okay, who can we put in this role?

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.280
But there as well you will
have the evaluation cycles

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.560
like this, that also work
somehow in this manner.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.570
So the HR leaders work together
with the business leaders,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.360
they're having a discussion,
and they ask themselves,

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.670
okay, who am I going to designate?

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:12.380
And usually how this works
if somebody prepares a case

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.874
for the individual who
then gets this cast,

00:05:14.874 --> 00:05:17.610
and kind of makes the case if he proposes

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.477
to designate the person, or not,

00:05:19.477 --> 00:05:22.445
and what the reasons
are, whether this person

00:05:22.445 --> 00:05:24.240
is worthwhile to get designated.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.140
And now think about the
role of this person.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.710
Usually it's a senior
leader in the organization,

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:33.730
he will have several more junior
colleagues working for him,

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.303
maybe not all of them are
directly working for himself,

00:05:36.303 --> 00:05:41.117
so he needs to reach out
to maybe an in between boss

00:05:41.117 --> 00:05:43.906
who then has more direct
exposure to the person,

00:05:43.906 --> 00:05:47.180
in order to understand if
this guy is a good guy or not.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.390
If this guy is worth getting designated.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.580
So often, in this kinds of situations,

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.460
the person actually makes
kind of a significant part

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.070
of the decision, namely by
making the recommendation

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.050
whether to designate the person or not,

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:02.400
is not even doing that based
on first-hand experience

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.990
working with the candidate,

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.700
but rather only maybe
drawing from hearsay.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.205
Drawing from conversations
he had with other people

00:06:10.205 --> 00:06:13.310
where actually you give a
more or less favorable review

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.140
of the individual or not.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.970
So what is actually visibility?

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:21.360
Visibility is how visible
you are, as the name says,

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.220
to the senior leaders in organization.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.190
Do they know that you exist?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:29.280
Does somebody maybe two
levels above your boss

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.580
know that you exist?

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.490
Does he know where your strengths are?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.820
Does he really know what you
did for the organization,

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.350
what the projects were
that you were working on?

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.010
How are you did in these projects?

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:43.510
What other initiatives might
be that you were driving?

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.740
And really how important you are

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.560
to the organization as a whole?

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:51.320
Is this visible to the
people to whom this matters,

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:55.330
namely the senior leaders in
the firm you're working in?

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.570
So now put yourself in
the shoes of a person

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.185
who needs to do these
kinds of review processes,

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:03.370
maybe he knows you a
little bit, maybe not,

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.820
but it becomes obvious
that how visible you are

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.390
to this person is super
crucial, and super important,

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.480
in the specific decision he needs to make

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:14.390
about what your future
is in the organization.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.370
And whether this needs a designation,

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.840
or any kind of other review process,

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.600
or other just perception that
the person has about you,

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.433
doesn't matter.

00:07:22.433 --> 00:07:24.500
But how visible you are to the person

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.610
clearly makes a huge difference
for you and your career.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:30.920
And while doing a good job
might be helpful for that,

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.500
might be a necessary condition for that,

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:34.910
it's not the only thing.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.872
And this alone, for sure,
will not make you visible

00:07:37.872 --> 00:07:40.860
to a person several steps up in the ladder

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.800
above your team lead, for instance,

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.550
because he just might see the
performance of the team lead,

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:47.280
and the team as a whole, and notice

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.907
actually it's going quite well.

00:07:48.907 --> 00:07:50.900
But it's very hard for him to judge,

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.950
just by looking at it outside in,

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.770
what the contribution of
individual team members

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:56.620
in the team might be,

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.900
that he then might also need to review.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.470
So is this a bit unfair?

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:02.760
Yes it is, for sure it's unfair.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.680
In a perfect world the only thing

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.500
that should matter is
how good you do your job.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.830
How reliable you are,

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.357
how well you deliver on the
things you're supposed to do,

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:14.230
this should be all that's relevant

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:16.000
when these things are decided.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.860
But the truth is it's
just not how this works.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.550
This is just not the truth,

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.570
just doing a good job alone won't do it.

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:25.840
In one sentence that is often described

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:29.210
in order to really make this
graspable is the sentence

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.156
perception is reality.

00:08:31.156 --> 00:08:33.910
Perception is reality.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.250
Think about that, what
really is the reality?

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:38.690
At least in such a business context,

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.610
is not so much what you really do.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.480
I mean you can sit at home
and then talk to your partner

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.363
all the things that you did,
and how great of a job you did,

00:08:46.363 --> 00:08:48.562
and how important you
are for the corporation,

00:08:48.562 --> 00:08:51.740
but if the perception
of everybody around you

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.720
is that that actually you're
not really doing a good job,

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.330
and you're not really adding
value to the business,

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.260
then this won't help you at all.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.633
Perception is reality.

00:09:00.633 --> 00:09:02.010
What you need to be good at,

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.770
and what you need to become good at,

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.760
is the management of the perceptions

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.290
of the people around you.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:09.560
And yes, for sure, this is politics.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.400
This is what is going on in
these large corporations.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.450
And this is also what makes
these places kind of annoying,

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.180
or maybe tiresome to work in,

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:20.440
because they are full
of politics like this.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.170
But the truth is also that
it's not necessarily better

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.490
in smaller organizations.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:25.820
In shades of gray, for sure,

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.390
but things like that happen everywhere.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:31.230
And if you want to be
successful in your job,

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.960
and I would say not only in your job

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.110
but almost everything you do in life,

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.800
in the end what matters is
understanding this principal

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.565
of perception is reality.

00:09:39.565 --> 00:09:42.270
Do a good job, this is the reality,

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.922
but make sure the other
people have the perception

00:09:44.922 --> 00:09:46.770
that you are actually doing a good job.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.377
Because if other people
do not perceive that,

00:09:49.377 --> 00:09:51.950
do not have the perception
that you are doing a good job,

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.660
then actually doing a good
job is no help for you at all.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.250
Especially in the context
where you're an employee

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:01.930
and do not directly benefit
from the results of your work.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.810
So now I'd like to give
you three tangible tips.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:07.430
What you can do, especially
if you are a new joiner,

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.970
if you are in a position
that you just started

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:11.100
your work life,

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.453
what you can do to actually
improve your visibility.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.660
So guys, if you're getting
value so far from this video,

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.310
please press the like button,

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.360
and please also subscribe to the channel

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.280
here on the subscribe button below,

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.210
in case you are not subscribed yet.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.500
This would mean a lot to me,

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.960
I have many more content planned

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.490
for the next days and weeks.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:32.323
Are you ready?

00:10:32.323 --> 00:10:33.156
Three tips.

00:10:33.156 --> 00:10:37.210
Number one, first clearly
communicate your successes.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.320
And very often we have this mentality

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.530
of maybe we are a bit shy,
we do not want to speak out

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.120
about what we actually
accomplished at work.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.550
What we actually did in
the last days or weeks,

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:49.420
because we feel like
we do not want to brag

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.670
about our achievements,
especially not towards your boss.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:55.180
Where you may be even afraid
that this is perceived

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:57.170
as arrogant, or something like that.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.070
And while this is very understandable,

00:11:03.683 --> 00:11:06.380
and for sure you need to be a
bit careful to not overdo it,

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:09.040
it's important that you
let other people know

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.410
if you did something great
that is really adding value

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:13.530
to the business or to your team.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:15.295
Do good things, and to talk about that.

00:11:15.295 --> 00:11:16.790
And this is an important principle.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:21.149
Don't just do good things
and then not talk about that,

00:11:21.149 --> 00:11:24.350
but do good things and then
do also talk about that

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.200
to your colleagues, to your boss.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.700
Not in a pretentious manner,

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.410
but rather just letting
them know what you did

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.690
in your next team meeting,

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.470
in your next one on one with the chief,

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:34.570
just recap with them the deliverables

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.410
that you accomplished in the last days.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.936
And just make sure that
it's really clear to them

00:11:38.936 --> 00:11:40.420
what you actually achieved,

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.670
what you got done in the last days,

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:44.240
don't just keep this to yourself

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:47.460
and just assume that
maybe over some other ways

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:50.570
they will know and understand
what the good things

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.250
and the skills are that you have.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:54.050
But aggressively let them know

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:56.070
about the good things that you do.

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:59.410
Because if you do not
advocate these things,

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.010
who else supposed to do that?

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:02.587
Maybe your colleagues say "Yes,

00:12:02.587 --> 00:12:03.707
"this guy he was really helpful,

00:12:03.707 --> 00:12:05.560
"and he helped me a lot in my work."

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:07.710
But I mean come on, you
cannot really rely on that.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.760
And again, perception is reality.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:11.640
It's not enough that you just do it,

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:14.390
but you need to make sure that
there's also the perception

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:16.095
on the other side of the table

00:12:16.095 --> 00:12:18.060
that you actually got these things done.

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:20.620
Because only then, this is
really adding value for you

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:23.190
in your career if you just do this.

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:25.370
The second tip is related to that,

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:28.530
and it's about how you
communicate your achievements

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:31.620
to your team colleagues, but
also to your supervisors.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:34.970
And there's a pretty
natural tendency, I'd say,

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:38.771
that if you work in a team
you always talk about we.

00:12:38.771 --> 00:12:41.940
We did this, we achieved this last week,

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:45.970
we worked on that, we got that
done, and so on and so forth.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:49.200
And while this is of course often fair,

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.920
while you often just want to make sure

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.620
that it will not take the compliments

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.500
for something that maybe not
you, but your team achieved,

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.688
very often this leads to the perception

00:12:57.688 --> 00:13:00.820
that actually your specific contribution

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:04.030
wasn't that large, but it
was rather a team effort.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.210
Everybody did something,

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.050
and yes of course you also did something,

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.310
but it was an effort of the team.

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:11.930
And I think what's important
here is to always also stress

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.810
what your specific contribution
to that result was.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.310
So yes, we can talk about
what you achieved as a team,

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:21.447
but then also say "I did
this, I worked on that.

00:13:21.447 --> 00:13:23.337
"Due to my efforts last week,

00:13:23.337 --> 00:13:25.677
"because I called somebody up last week,

00:13:25.677 --> 00:13:27.630
"this is then what happened."

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:30.321
And this is not about
you making something up.

00:13:30.321 --> 00:13:33.910
This is not about something
else, or somebody else did it,

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.440
and then you just claimed that you did it.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:36.620
This is of course not at all

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.380
what I'm recommending you to do.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.470
But the many things that you did do,

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:43.510
the many things where you
really did take ownership,

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:45.660
and did make an effort to really bring

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.500
that success to the
team, make it transparent

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.810
that this actually was your contribution,

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:52.620
that you actually did that.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.940
And I think this is an insider
tip that not only applies

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:00.616
to how you communicate,
but also in for instance

00:14:00.616 --> 00:14:03.324
written applications,
or even job interviews,

00:14:03.324 --> 00:14:05.530
if you're now supposed to describe

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:06.930
what you achieved in the past,

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.767
here again it's very
common for people to say

00:14:08.767 --> 00:14:11.460
"We did this, we did that," and so on.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.000
And then for you as an intern,

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.458
if you try to put yourself in
the shoes of the other guy,

00:14:15.458 --> 00:14:16.850
it's really hard to understand,

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:20.140
okay, but this guy, Heinrich,
what did he really achieve?

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:21.945
What can he do for us?

00:14:21.945 --> 00:14:25.610
So also always stress not
only what the team result was,

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:30.060
but what your specific contribution
to that result has been.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.718
Just to make that visible and
also create the impression

00:14:32.718 --> 00:14:35.890
that you as a person really
add value to the team.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.740
My third tip is to pick up initiative,

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:43.550
and organize some things beyond
your daily, day-to-day job.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:45.340
And what do I mean by that?

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.240
Often in a team or in an organization

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.740
there are things where you can volunteer,

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.950
or where you can take the
lead and do something,

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.430
which might not directly
be expected from you.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.910
Or it might not be that
your team comes to you

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.620
and tells you "Heinrich,
this what I want you to do."

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.740
But still it just adds value to the team,

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:04.140
and if only to the spirit,

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:06.460
and to kind of the team
feeling as a whole.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:07.870
And some examples here could be

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:10.330
that you for instance
organize a team event.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.410
You just organize an event for your team,

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.830
where then you organization everything,

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:17.160
and then the team goes maybe
to an offsite in the evening,

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.230
or somewhere else, just
to have a good time.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.830
And then hopefully everybody
comes back in the office

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:24.610
the next day and it
feels like a more bonded,

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.070
a better team to everybody.

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.320
This could be one example.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.910
Or maybe you organize
some kind of sports event

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:31.550
in your office, or you take ownership

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:34.460
of any kind of other
initiative that is going on.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.920
So these are little things where

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:39.010
this is likely going beyond your job,

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:41.000
this is not directly expected from you,

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.350
but you show ownership,
you show initiative,

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.180
you show that you want to contribute

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:49.160
beyond what is necessarily
directly expected from you.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.980
And by that this will be visible.

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:54.290
If now you have a team
lead and now he will see

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.030
that the team is gone to a team event,

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.280
with or without him,

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.040
he will very quickly pick up
who that was who organized that

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.290
and who made this effort for better

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.200
team experience for everybody.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.340
And of course, your main roads,
your main responsibilities

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:08.810
will always be more important.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:11.600
Don't do these things
they put you in danger

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:13.650
of actually delivering against the things

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:14.870
that you're really supposed to do,

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.820
or that are really expected from you.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:20.000
Because if you do that then
it doesn't really matter

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.766
if you organized the great team event,

00:16:21.766 --> 00:16:23.970
if your actual job is not done right.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.420
So prioritize correctly, but very often

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.653
you will find yourself
having a bit of spare time,

00:16:28.653 --> 00:16:30.730
having a bit of extra capacity

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.950
that you could invest in
these kinds of things,

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:35.130
and then it is super
valuable if you do that.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:37.650
If you take initiative, take leadership.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:40.140
And then do something
good for the organization,

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.720
this will be recognized.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.600
And this for sure will put you on the list

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.440
of these more seniors leaders,

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:48.400
and then make you more visible to them.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.440
So let's recap, visibility
is super important,

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.080
and it means how visible you
are to the senior leaders

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.500
in your organization.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.260
Do they know that you exist?

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:00.900
Do they know what you
are doing for the team?

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:03.250
Do they know why you really add value

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.883
to their organization as a whole?

00:17:04.883 --> 00:17:06.641
Perception is reality.

00:17:06.641 --> 00:17:07.640
It doesn't matter,

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.850
it's not enough if you do just a good job,

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:12.030
you need to make sure that
other people understand

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:14.160
and perceive that you do a good job.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.140
Otherwise it's just not worth a lot.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.150
So make sure that this
perception is there.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.860
Make sure that you are visible.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.410
I hope that if you follow these tips,

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:22.700
that this will help you.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:26.170
And if you really enjoyed this
please click the like button

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.190
